-- title:
--   G Hat Facts
-- statement:
--   **A good strategy with consistent bounded slices satisfies the two G-hat facts.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric projective strategy for the successor space and let $G^x$ be a slice-indexed family of projective polynomial submeasurements. Assume that $S$ is good with errors $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma$, that the family is point-consistent with $S$ at error $\zeta$, and that it is strongly self-consistent with the state of $S$ at the same error. Assume also the nonnegative slice-boundedness witnesses required to control the residual operators, together with $0\le\gamma\le1$, $0\le\zeta\le1$, and $d\le q$.
--
--   Then the completed G-hat family satisfies the self-consistency relation
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDRel}_{\psi,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)}(\widehat G_{\mathrm{left}},\widehat G_{\mathrm{right}};2\zeta),
--   $$
--
--   and the pair-product commutation relation
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^2)}
--   \left(\widehat G_{\mathrm{pair,left}},\widehat G_{\mathrm{pair,right}};
--   138m\left(\operatorname{rpow}(\gamma,1/16)+\operatorname{rpow}(\zeta,1/16)+\operatorname{rpow}(d/q,1/16)\right)\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the source-facing G-hat-facts result: the goodness, point consistency, strong self-consistency, and boundedness assumptions supply the component estimates needed for both completed-family conclusions.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.gHatFacts`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/GHatFacts.lean#L502-L530

